R CMD INSTALL: build the native library with rzig build (zig build alone)

Before the make path, run_shlib asks R_HOME/bin/toolchain/rzig to build
the package's library: `rzig build` classifies the package (no
src/Makefile, which install.R runs with make before it gets here, and
its own src/build.zig, or no configure and a Makevars of assignments
only [code-2]), derives from etc/Makeconf and the Makevars the compile
and link lines make would have run, and runs them as zig build steps
that call the same compilers (zig-cc, zig-cxx, zig-fc). The library
lands in src/ as make's does, and shlib_install() takes it from there
(install.libs.R, strip, dSYM as before). Exit 3 means the package needs
make, and the make path runs unchanged. On unix rzig is started with
.Internal(spawnWait()) (patch 0012), no shell; on Windows system2()
spawns without one already. R_ZIG_PKG_BUILDER=auto|zig|make chooses
(zig: an error where the hook would hand the package to make, a tier-3
package or a toolchain with no rzig [preflight-PF-4]; make: rzig is
never asked), for parity runs and bisecting. R_ZIG_JOBS, else
MAKEFLAGS' -j, is the job count; a variable assignment in MAKEFLAGS
makes rzig build decline a package make can build (make's build would
differ). A src/build.zig package has no make build: one whose build
would need make anyway fails, exit 1, after rzig's line "<pkg>:
src/build.zig cannot be built by make: <reason>", instead of a make
path that ignores build.zig [preflight-PF-1]. rzig reads the user
Makevars R found: the hook passes makevars_user() as R_MAKEVARS_USER
when it names a file, since R's `~` falls back to the passwd home when
HOME is unset and rzig's does not [code-5]. A src/build.zig alone (a
zig package, no C source) counts as compiled code. patch_rpaths reads
the OS from Sys.info() instead of `uname -a`. The install preflight
(patch 0009) decides the tier the same way, before configure, through
`--rzig-check=package`. CC's binary beside no rzig name (a toolchain
older than this R) is an error, not a silent make path.
.github/devdocs/feat-zig-pkg-build/PLAN.md, milestone 3 and the
consolidation with phase 3.

